3. TTL (Time To Live)
First fundamental concept.
________________________________________
Problem
Suppose CDN stores:
logo.png
Forever.
One day logo changes.
Users still see old version.
Bad.
________________________________________
Need expiration.
________________________________________
TTL means:
How long cache is valid.
Example:
HTTP
Cache-Control: max-age=3600
Meaning:
3600 seconds= 1 hour
________________________________________
After 1 hour: Cache expires
Need verification or re-fetch.
________________________________________
Internal Data Structure
CDN stores:
class CachedObject {
byte[] content;
long expiryTime;
}
Request:
if(now < expiryTime)
Serve cache.
Otherwise:
Expired
Revalidate.
________________________________________
4. Cache-Control Header
Most important HTTP caching header.
________________________________________
Why Invented?
Before HTTP/1.1:
Caching behavior inconsistent
Different browsers behaved differently.
Needed standard rules.
________________________________________
Example
HTTP
Cache-Control: max-age=3600
Meaning: Keep for 1 hour.
________________________________________
Common Directives
________________________________________
max-age
HTTP
Cache-Control: max-age=3600
Fresh for: 1 hour
________________________________________
no-cache
Many developers misunderstand this.
It DOES NOT mean:
Don't cache
It means:
Cache it BUT verify before reuse
________________________________________
Request flow:
Browser
↓
Server Verification
↓
Reuse if unchanged
________________________________________
no-store
Real meaning:
Never store
Examples:
Banking
Payments
OTP
________________________________________
private
Only browser cache.
HTTP
Cache-Control: private
CDN should not cache.
________________________________________
Example:
User profile page
________________________________________
public
Anyone may cache.
HTTP
Cache-Control: public
Perfect for:
CSS
JS
Images
Videos
________________________________________
Example
HTTP
Cache-Control: public,max-age=86400
Meaning:
Cache publicly
For 24 hours
________________________________________
5. Fresh vs Stale Content
Critical concept.
________________________________________
Fresh
Current time:
10:00 AM
Expiry:
11:00 AM
Request arrives:
10:30 AM
Fresh.
Serve immediately.
________________________________________
Stale
Current time:
11:30 AM
Expired.
Need revalidation.
________________________________________
Visual:
Created
↓
Fresh
↓
Fresh
↓
Fresh
↓
Expired
