6. ETag (Entity Tag)
One of the most important concepts in web engineering.
________________________________________
The Problem
Suppose:
movie.jpg
is:
20 MB
Browser has copy.
After TTL expires:
Should browser download entire 20 MB again?
Wasteful.
________________________________________
Need way to ask:
Has file changed?
without downloading file.
________________________________________
Solution
Server gives fingerprint.
Example:
HTTP
ETag: "abc123"
Think of it as:
File Version Hash
________________________________________
First Request
Server:
HTTP
200 OK
ETag: "abc123"
Browser stores:
File
ETag
________________________________________
Second Request
Browser sends:
HTTP
If-None-Match: "abc123"
Meaning:
I already have this.
Has it changed?
________________________________________
Server Checks
If unchanged:
HTTP
304 Not Modified
No file sent.
Only tiny response.
________________________________________
If changed:
HTTP
200 OK
ETag: "xyz999"
New file downloaded.
________________________________________
Request Flow
Browser
↓
If-None-Match: abc123
↓
Origin
________________________________________
If same:
304 Not Modified
________________________________________
Bandwidth:
Few bytes
instead of 20 MB

Huge savings.
________________________________________
7. Last-Modified
Older mechanism.
________________________________________
Instead of hash:
Store timestamp.
Example:
HTTP
Last-Modified:
Mon, 01 Jan 2025 10:00:00 GMt
________________________________________
Browser later sends:
HTTP
If-Modified-Since:
Mon, 01 Jan 2025 10:00:00 GMT
________________________________________
Server checks.
Unchanged:
HTTP
304 Not Modified
________________________________________
Changed:
HTTP
200 OK
Send file.
________________________________________
ETag vs Last-Modified
Feature	ETag	Last-Modified
Accuracy	High	Medium
Uses Hash/Version	Yes	No
Uses Timestamp	No	Yes
Detects Tiny Changes	Yes	Sometimes Not
Industry Preference	Preferred	Secondary
________________________________________
8. 304 Not Modified
One of the most important HTTP responses.
________________________________________
Without 304:
20 MB Download
Every time.
________________________________________
With 304:
Small Response
Use Existing File
________________________________________
Example:
HTTP
HTTP/1.1 304 Not Modified
Browser:
Use local copy
________________________________________
Benefits:
Lower Bandwidth
Lower Latency
Lower CDN Cost
Lower Origin Cost
________________________________________
