Final 
Think of a CDN as five distributed systems combined:

1. DNS System
2. Routing System
(Anycast + BGP)
3. Distributed Cache
(TTL, ETag, Keys)
4. Security Platform
(TLS, WAF, DDoS)
5. Replication System
(Invalidation, Purging)
If you truly understand Lessons 1-9, you're already beyond what many 6-8 year engineers know about CDNs.
